# Shop name in Optima Regular (HARD — Founder Oct 30, 2026)

On awnings, windows, signs, and any place the shop name appears: **set SACRED GROUND in Optima Regular**, tight, like the Saturn lockup. Do **not** paste or stretch the long / stacked logo PNGs.

The image model still must never invent the letters. That is how plates come back as SACREED / GROUNDD / REALED.

## The lock (Founder Oct 30, 2026)

| Do this | Not this |
|---|---|
| **Optima Regular** — `SACRED GROUND` as one tight lockup | Paste / stretch `sacred-ground-logo-long.png` (21848) or stacked (21849) onto a fascia |
| Words together — same tightness as Saturn | Wide gap between SACRED and GROUND |
| Tip the type to the roof / awning when the photo is angled (S up, far end down) | Level type on a sloped roof |
| Leave the awning blank in the generation, then set the type | Ask the model to paint the name, or pass 21848 / 21849 as `selectedImages` for it to copy |

Circular sun (`sacred-ground-logo-circle-transparent.png`) stays the **corner mark** only.

## How to put the name on a plate

1. Generation: awning / window / sign stays **blank**. No shop-name letters in the prompt.
2. Design pass: **Optima Regular** (`/System/Library/Fonts/Optima.ttc` on this Mac). Tracking tight. One space, not a stretched sticker.
3. If the building is angled, rotate the lockup a little so it sits on the fascia.
4. Optional gold wave only if the words stay together. If the wave opens a hole, drop the wave and keep the type tight.

## Campaign sentences on dark plates

Large type, **Sacred Ground gold** `(238, 191, 42)` — not white on a busy night photo. Aliens 04 headline is the read.

